DESCRIPTION:National American Teddy Bear Day is marked on November 14\, the
  date in 1902 when Theodore Roosevelt went bear hunting in Mississippi and
  refused to shoot the animal his hosts had cornered for him. The observanc
 e's own origin is undocumented\; the hunt behind it is not. What followed 
 was a newspaper cartoon\, a Brooklyn candy shop\, and the only American to
 y named after a president.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/national
 -american-teddy-bear-day/
